    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/digital-to-wave-2-debroglie"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC matter-wave test of the object hologram claimed in Mun Seok
  Lee's preprint "Digital to Wave: LGD In Situ Wave Memory-Human Wave
  Integrated Interface-Metaverse Hologram- Wave Affective AI" (Part II).
  It applies the relativistic de Broglie wavelength, lambda = h /
  sqrt(2 m E + E^2 / c^2) — the paper's own formula, correctly stated
  there — to the paper's own numbers (CMB peculiar velocity 370 km/s,
  LGD lattice pitch 0.356 nm, THz band 300 GHz - 3 THz) and computes
  the matter wavelength for electron, proton, 1 kg, 70 kg and 1000 kg
  masses at the CMB velocity and at thermal velocity (300 K), the
  ratios to the THz wavelength and to the lattice pitch, the phase
  across one lattice spacing, and the mass whose matter wavelength
  would equal the THz wavelength. Verdict: FAIL. For 70 kg at
  370 km/s the matter wavelength is 2.56 x 10^-41 m, 1.17 x 10^37
  times shorter than the 1 THz wavelength, with a phase of 8.74 x
  10^31 rad across one lattice spacing. No physical, biological or
  safety claim is made. The preprint's author has not reviewed or
  endorsed this software. DOI pending (no Zenodo record yet).
keywords:
